title: The Campaign
subtitle: Germany elects its first Reichstag on 6 June.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 5 and crisis = 0 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2

= The Campaign

The first Reichstag of the Republic will be elected on 6 June. [? if kapp_outcome = 3 : The workers' government hopes for a majority of its own, and the bourgeois parties campaign against "the dictatorship of Legien". ?][? if kapp_outcome = 1 : The coalition of the SPD, the Centre and the Democrats is tired. The nationalists campaign on Versailles, the Independents on the betrayal of the revolution. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 2 : The election is held under the guns of the generals who nearly took the country. ?]

We have few candidates anyone has heard of, and no daily paper in most of the Reich. [? if election_boycott = 1 : The party has decided to boycott the vote. ?]

- @lessons: Campaign on who stopped Kapp.
- @bloc: Call for a bloc of the workers' parties.
- @boycott: Boycott the election.

@lessons
subtitle: The strikers of March will listen.
choose-if: lock_elections < 2 and election_boycott = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The party will not stand in this election.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_campaign = 1;
Q.election_bonus += Q.kapp_statement == 1 ? 1 : 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Our posters show the Ehrhardt Brigade's helmets and the strikers who stopped them. [? if kapp_statement = 1 : Hecklers read out our statement of 13 March at every meeting. ?]

@bloc
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The USPD will like it. Some of our voters will go to them.
choose-if: lock_elections < 2 and election_boycott = 0 and lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The party line does not allow it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e20_campaign = 3;
Q.election_bonus += 1;
Q.uspd_relation += 8;
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Our speakers call for a workers' majority in the Reichstag. The USPD's speakers say kind things about us for the first time.

@boycott
subtitle: No votes for parliament, our own included.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0 or election_boycott = 1 or lock_elections = 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_campaign = 4;
Q.election_boycott = 1;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 10;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 1;
!}

Our posters say: do not vote, organise in the factories. Most workers vote anyway, for the USPD.
